# What Vercel must NOT upload.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every git-push deployment of this repo failed, for weeks,
# with:
#
#     LAMBDA_SIZE_EXCEEDED
#     Total bundle size (516.86 MB) exceeds the maximum function size (500 MB)
#
# Vercel treats the REPO ROOT as the deployment root (root vercel.json builds the
# frontend, but it does not move the root). It therefore auto-detects
# `api/compute/size.py` as a Python serverless function and installs the root
# `requirements.txt` to build it — cvxpy with its solver binaries, plus scipy,
# pandas, numpy and yfinance. That is 516.86 MB before any of our code, and the
# ceiling is 500 MB.
#
# The failure was invisible for two reasons worth recording. CI runs pytest only,
# so a red Vercel build never fails a check; and the live site kept working
# because it was being served by a MANUAL `vercel deploy` from `frontend/`, which
# never sees `api/`. So `main` was undeployable while the URL looked healthy.
#
# WHAT EXCLUDING `api/` COSTS, precisely: nothing that currently works. ADR-0149
# shipped `api/compute/size.py` labelled "NOT YET DEPLOYED: first deploy must
# reproduce published weights bit-for-bit" — and it never has been deployed,
# because of this exact limit. Excluding it makes that state explicit instead of
# leaving it as a build that fails every night. `Workbench.tsx` fetches
# `/api/compute/size` and will 404, which is what it already does in production.
#
# The real fix is one of:
#   1. set the Vercel project's Root Directory to `frontend`, so Vercel never
#      sees the Python tree at all (cleanest — a dashboard setting, not a file);
#   2. drop `yfinance` from requirements.txt, which needs `book_metrics` to split
#      its asset records from its price helpers — requirements.txt's own comment
#      already names this as the blocker;
#   3. move the solver behind a service that is not a 500 MB lambda.
# Until one of those happens, this file is what makes `main` deployable.

# The Python serverless function and its dependency manifest.
api/
requirements.txt

# The pipeline. Never served; only inflates the upload.
backend/
scripts/
tests/
supabase/

# Documentation, research and scratch. Not part of any build.
docs/
research/
email/
stitch_review/
stitch_remix_of_auralis_saas_landing_page/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv-*/

# Large binaries that must never reach a deployment.
*.zip
*.pdf
